 "text": "Hi there, how are you doing these days? That's a bit of a stuck point. French intermediate is often stuck in one way of doing things. Have you tried a good vocabulary builder app? They' pretty accurate without being too glossy. Lots of synonyms, antonyms and expressions you can actually use. In the short term, yes. Use it for two weeks and you' find your head speed up. Try it after each work day when your mind is ready for a nibble. You can correct them as you go, and a few minutes day will make a real difference. If you' rather not look at screen, there are books too. That' pays off a lot. A few words every day, and you' find them turn up without you realising.",
